{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/bash -lc \"cat .pose/rules/backend-go.md; sed -n '898,1025p' pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate.go; sed -n '1,130p' .pose/indexes/validation-matrix.json; rg -n 'script|subcommand|subcomando|recurs|hook' POSE.md | tail -12; ls /var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-15067286; rg -n 'func .*ArtifactPath|symlink escapes|symlink' pose-mcp/internal/pose/delivery_integrity_test.go | head -25\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/bash -lc \"cat .pose/rules/backend-go.md; sed -n '898,1025p' pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate.go; sed -n '1,130p' .pose/indexes/validation-matrix.json; rg -n 'script|subcommand|subcomando|recurs|hook' POSE.md | tail -12; ls /var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-15067286; rg -n 'func .*ArtifactPath|symlink escapes|symlink' pose-mcp/internal/pose/delivery_integrity_test.go | head -25\"","aggregated_output":"# Rule: Backend Go\n\n## When to consult\n\nConsult this guide for HTTP handlers, domain services, persistence, concurrency, and integrations between Go services.\n\n## Required patterns\n\n- Handle and propagate errors with enough context for diagnosis.\n- Validate handler input and return HTTP status codes consistent with the contract.\n- Keep business rules in service or domain layers, not in transport code.\n- Honor `context.Context` for timeouts and cancellation.\n- Put data access behind clear interfaces that support testing.\n- Use structured logs without exposing sensitive data.\n\n## Blocking anti-patterns\n\n- Ignoring error returns, including `_` for critical errors.\n- Using `panic` in ordinary request flows instead of controlled error handling.\n- Coupling handlers directly to concrete repository implementations without an abstraction.\n- Running unbounded or unpaginated queries in potentially large endpoints.\n- Introducing concurrency without adequate synchronization or race protection.\n\n## Minimum checks\n\n- Run `go test ./...` in the affected scope.\n- Run `go test -race ./...` when concurrency changes.\n- Run `go vet ./...` without blocking findings.\n- Run the applicable Go lint check, such as `golangci-lint`, without critical errors.\n\n## Precedence in multi-domain conflicts\n\n- Apply the most restrictive security, contract, and operational rule when domain rules conflict.\n- Prefer verifiable check evidence and explicit risk mitigation when speed conflicts with control.\n- Record the precedence decision and objective rationale in the review.\n\n## Recurrence traceability\n\n> Also apply: [.pose/rules/_base-recurrence.md](_base-recurrence.md)\nfunc cmdValidateWithStore(store posemodel.Store, args []string, stdout, stderr io.Writer) int {\n\troot := store.Root\n\tlocale := cliLocaleValue()\n\tmode, stackFilter, moduleFilter, reportTask := \"\", \"\", \"\", \"\"\n\tjsonOut, junitOut, sarifOut, planOut := \"\", \"\", \"\", \"\"\n\tchangedFrom, changedTo := \"\", \"\"\n\texplain := false\n\tverbose := false\n\tautoReport := false\n\trootOnly := false\n\tworkspaceFilter := \"\"\n\tjobs := 0\n\tvar isolationChecks []checkResult\n\tfor i := 0; i < len(args); i++ {\n\t\tswitch args[i] {\n\t\tcase \"--strict\":\n\t\t\tmode = \"strict\"\n\t\tcase \"--tolerant\":\n\t\t\tmode = \"tolerant\"\n\t\tcase \"--report\":\n\t\t\tautoReport = true\n\t\tcase \"--explain\":\n\t\t\texplain = true\n\t\tcase \"--verbose\":\n\t\t\t// A check's output is captured by default; --verbose streams it\n\t\t\t// (spec pose-cli-output-rendering-system R7).\n\t\t\tverbose = true\n\t\tcase \"--root-only\":\n\t\t\t// Documented alias of --module . (spec\n\t\t\t// pose-monorepo-validation-advisory, R2) — sugar over the\n\t\t\t// existing selector, no new selection logic.\n\t\t\trootOnly = true\n\t\tcase \"--stack\", \"--module\", \"--workspace\", \"--report-task\", \"--json\", \"--json-out\", \"--junit\", \"--sarif\", \"--emit-plan\", \"--changed-from\", \"--changed-to\", \"--jobs\":\n\t\t\tif i+1 >= len(args) || strings.HasPrefix(args[i+1], \"--\") {\n\t\t\t\tfmt.Fprintf(stderr, cliText(locale, \"Error: %s requires a value.\\n\", \"Erro: %s exige um valor.\\n\"), args[i])\n\t\t\t\treturn 2\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t\ti++\n\t\t\tswitch args[i-1] {\n\t\t\tcase \"--jobs\":\n\t\t\t\tn, err := strconv.Atoi(args[i])\n\t\t\t\tif err != nil || n < 1 {\n\t\t\t\t\trender(stdout, stderr).Failure(cliText(locale, \"--jobs must be a positive integer\", \"--jobs deve ser um inteiro positivo\"))\n\t\t\t\t\treturn 2\n\t\t\t\t}\n\t\t\t\tjobs = n\n\t\t\tcase \"--stack\":\n\t\t\t\tstackFilter = args[i]\n\t\t\tcase \"--module\":\n\t\t\t\tmoduleFilter = filepath.ToSlash(filepath.Clean(args[i]))\n\t\t\tcase \"--workspace\":\n\t\t\t\t// Documented alias of --module <path> (R3) that resolves a\n\t\t\t\t// package/crate name to its module path, for the case\n\t\t\t\t// where the operator knows the workspace member's name but\n\t\t\t\t// not its relative directory.\n\t\t\t\tworkspaceFilter = args[i]\n\t\t\tcase \"--report-task\":\n\t\t\t\treportTask = args[i]\n\t\t\tcase \"--json-out\":\n\t\t\t\tjsonOut = args[i]\n\t\t\tcase \"--json\":\n\t\t\t\t// Everywhere else --json prints to stdout; here it named a file.\n\t\t\t\t// It keeps working, announced as deprecated (spec\n\t\t\t\t// pose-cli-output-machine-channel, R2).\n\t\t\t\tjsonOut = args[i]\n\t\t\t\trender(stdout, stderr).Hint(cliText(locale, \"validate --json <path> is deprecated; use --json-out <path>.\", \"validate --json <path> está depreciado; use --json-out <path>.\"))\n\t\t\tcase \"--junit\":\n\t\t\t\tjunitOut = args[i]\n\t\t\tcase \"--sarif\":\n\t\t\t\tsarifOut = args[i]\n\t\t\tcase \"--emit-plan\":\n\t\t\t\tplanOut = args[i]\n\t\t\tcase \"--changed-from\":\n\t\t\t\tchangedFrom = args[i]\n\t\t\tcase \"--changed-to\":\n\t\t\t\tchangedTo = args[i]\n\t\t\t}\n\t\tdefault:\n\t\t\tfmt.Fprintf(stderr, cliText(locale, \"Error: invalid argument: %s\\n\", \"Erro: argumento inválido: %s\\n\"), args[i])\n\t\t\treturn 2\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\tif rootOnly && moduleFilter != \"\" {\n\t\tfmt.Fprintln(stderr, cliText(locale, \"Error: --root-only and --module are mutually exclusive.\", \"Erro: --root-only e --module são mutuamente exclusivos.\"))\n\t\treturn 2\n\t}\n\tif workspaceFilter != \"\" && (moduleFilter != \"\" || rootOnly) {\n\t\tfmt.Fprintln(stderr, cliText(locale, \"Error: --workspace, --module and --root-only are mutually exclusive.\", \"Erro: --workspace, --module e --root-only são mutuamente exclusivos.\"))\n\t\treturn 2\n\t}\n\tif rootOnly {\n\t\tmoduleFilter = \".\"\n\t}\n\tfor _, out := range []string{jsonOut, junitOut, sarifOut, planOut} {\n\t\tif out != \"\" && !confinedRelativePath(out) {\n\t\t\tfmt.Fprintln(stderr, cliText(locale, \"Error: result output paths must remain inside the project.\", \"Erro: paths de saída de resultado devem permanecer dentro do projeto.\"))\n\t\t\treturn 2\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\tcanonicalResultsPath := \"\"\n\tif jsonOut != \"\" {\n\t\tcanonicalResultsPath = configuredDeliveryResultsPath(root)\n\t}\n\t// The report --report writes records this run, so it reads this run's own\n\t// output. It used to look for a pose-validate.latest.log that native\n\t// validation never writes, and every report said \"Fill manually\" and \"No\n\t// validation output detected\" under an outcome it could not support (spec\n\t// pose-validate-report-carries-its-run).\n\t// The report records this run from the run's own structured result, not\n\t// from its printed output (spec pose-cli-output-rendering-system R5).\n\t// Capturing stdout to re-parse it is what made every printed line a\n\t// contract.\n\tif stackFilter != \"\" && !map[string]bool{\"node\": true, \"go\": true, \"rust\": true, \"java\": true, \"python\": true, \"dotnet\": true, \"contract\": true}[stackFilter] {\n\t\tfmt.Fprintf(stderr, cliText(locale, \"Error: invalid --stack: %s\\n\", \"Erro: --stack inválido: %s\\n\"), stackFilter)\n\t\treturn 2\n\t}\n\tif moduleFilter == \"..\" || strings.HasPrefix(moduleFilter, \"../\") || filepath.IsAbs(moduleFilter) {\n\t\tfmt.Fprintln(stderr, cliText(locale, \"Error: --module must remain inside the project.\", \"Erro: --module deve permanecer dentro do projeto.\"))\n\t\treturn 2\n\t}\n\tmatrixPath := filepath.Join(root, \".pose\", \"indexes\", \"validation-matrix.json\")\n\traw, err := os.ReadFile(matrixPath)\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\tfmt.Fprintf(stderr, cliText(locale, \"Error: validation matrix not found at %s\\n\", \"Erro: matriz de validação não encontrada em %s\\n\"), matrixPath)\n\t\treturn 2\n\t}\n\tmatrix, err := parseValidationMatrix(raw)\n\tif err != nil {\n{\n  \"defaults\": {\n    \"mode\": \"strict\"\n  },\n  \"deliveryProfiles\": {\n    \"cli-surface\": {\n      \"kind\": \"surface\",\n      \"requiredEvidenceClasses\": [\n        \"reachability\"\n      ],\n      \"anyEvidenceClasses\": [\n        \"integration\",\n        \"e2e\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"composed-capability\": {\n      \"kind\": \"capability\",\n      \"requiredEvidenceClasses\": [\n        \"integration\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"api-contract\": {\n      \"kind\": \"contract\",\n      \"requiredEvidenceClasses\": [\n        \"integration\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"release-governance\": {\n      \"kind\": \"governance\",\n      \"requiredEvidenceClasses\": [\n        \"integration\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"backend-go\": {\n      \"kind\": \"governance\",\n      \"requiredEvidenceClasses\": [\n        \"integration\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"structural-delta\": {\n      \"kind\": \"governance\",\n      \"requiredEvidenceClasses\": [\n        \"integration\"\n      ]\n    }\n  },\n  \"stacks\": {\n    \"node\": {\n      \"checks\": [\n        {\n          \"name\": \"lint\",\n          \"program\": \"npm\",\n          \"args\": [\n            \"run\",\n            \"lint\",\n            \"--if-present\"\n          ],\n          \"severity\": \"optional\",\n          \"evidenceClass\": \"lint\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"test\",\n          \"program\": \"npm\",\n          \"args\": [\n            \"test\",\n            \"--if-present\"\n          ],\n          \"severity\": \"required\",\n          \"evidenceClass\": \"unit\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"build\",\n          \"program\": \"npm\",\n          \"args\": [\n            \"run\",\n            \"build\",\n            \"--if-present\"\n          ],\n          \"severity\": \"required\",\n          \"evidenceClass\": \"build\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"typecheck\",\n          \"program\": \"npm\",\n          \"args\": [\n            \"run\",\n            \"typecheck\",\n            \"--if-present\"\n          ],\n          \"severity\": \"optional\",\n          \"evidenceClass\": \"typecheck\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    \"go\": {\n      \"checks\": [\n        {\n          \"name\": \"build\",\n          \"program\": \"go\",\n          \"args\": [\n            \"build\",\n            \"./...\"\n          ],\n          \"severity\": \"required\",\n          \"evidenceClass\": \"build\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"test\",\n          \"program\": \"go\",\n          \"args\": [\n            \"test\",\n            \"./...\"\n          ],\n          \"severity\": \"required\",\n          \"evidenceClass\": \"unit\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"vet\",\n          \"program\": \"go\",\n          \"args\": [\n            \"vet\",\n            \"./...\"\n          ],\n          \"severity\": \"optional\",\n          \"evidenceClass\": \"lint\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    \"rust\": {\n      \"checks\": [\n946:Reservations live in `.pose/review-attempts/`, final receipts link the run, and `.pose/review-run-ledger/` witnesses exact run bytes and transcript digests. Every publication uses the exclusive synced publisher. New runs carry `ledger_version: 1`, `attempt_id` and the optional reason; legacy schema-1 runs retain their original identities, with no invented reservation or signature. An incomplete reservation, missing witness/run/transcript, inconsistent receipt, unknown record or exhausted read budget is explicitly incomplete. Inspect it; no automatic deletion, truncation, repair or retry occurs. Upgrade writers sharing these directories together. Run continuity and authenticated provenance remain separate deliveries.\n948:`pose history-check --strict` detects missing or rewritten witnessed runs and Git modifications/deletions of tracked immutable run, ledger and attempt files, including staged or committed changes. History containing only delegated records is supported. Git/filesystem trust is required: erasing unanchored evidence and its witnesses cannot be proved from that same erased storage. No cryptographic append-only storage or vendor identity is claimed. Records are limited to 1 MiB, inventories to 10000 entries, run JSON reads to 32 MiB per operation, transcripts to 256 MiB each and 512 MiB per verification, and Git history observation to 8 MiB/30 seconds; exceeding a bound is unknown, never a clean truncated history.\n956:**Delegated runs over MCP.** `pose_delegate_start` (review, adjudicate or smoke), `pose_delegate_status`, `pose_delegate_wait`, `pose_delegate_resume` and `pose_delegate_handoff` run `pose delegate … --json` in the project the server resolved for the call, so every plan, refusal and run is the CLI's: a start, resume or handoff is always detached and returns once the run has reserved its attempt (without `apply` it previews), a status never blocks, and a wait blocks at most its `timeout_seconds` (300 at most), returning `still-running` when the bound passes. Refusals carry the same `reason_code` as the CLI's error document (`rerun-without-reason`, `budget-exhausted`, `containment-incompatible`, `agent-unavailable`, `no-agent`), and results carry the normalized summary only: no transcript, prompt, session reference or environment value. `pose delegate resume` and `handoff` take `--detach` as the purposes do. A task is not started over MCP.\n962:and excerpts; keep full transcripts and command output in files. Use the native\n1017:Keep environment/credentials lists unique ignoring case (at most 128/32 names). Ambient token variables are excluded. Explicit profiles use a private disposable HOME; an omitted profile is disclosed as `legacy-trusted` and retains HOME compatibility. This is environment filtering, not protection against an executable reading same-user files. Authorize credential variable names explicitly; never put their values in policy, argv, brief or notes. Loader hooks and Git redirection variables cannot be allowlisted. Credential values and captured session references are redacted together in one bounded pass, longest match first; this is exact-value redaction, not general data-loss prevention or a guarantee against encoded secrets emitted by an untrusted adapter.\n1019:Use a positive timeout from 1ms to 24h (omitted: 60m). Omit `max_runs_per_bundle` for a finite default of three; explicit values must be 1..100, including on legacy adapters. Explicit zero/null is invalid. Omitted stream/output/retained limits are 8MiB/64KiB/16MiB; explicit ranges are 1..64MiB, 1..128KiB and 1..128MiB. Require retained bytes to cover `stream_bytes + 6*output_bytes + 1048576` for JSON escaping and metadata. The retained budget covers the run record plus transcript per execution; independent bounded ledger/proof inventories still apply. It is not an aggregate storage quota, an adapter memory quota or an OS disk limit. Memory/CPU settings, positive TTL and unknown enforcement fields are refused by this backend.\n1021:Bound setup to two minutes and 64KiB of discarded diagnostic capture; disable ambient checkout hooks. Bound concurrent stdout/stderr together during capture and read `{output}` through a root descriptor opened before spawn, refusing links, special files, identity changes and oversized files. Notes must be regular non-symlink UTF-8 files up to 16KiB. Do not interpolate brief/notes into shell code. Truncated, unsafe or unredactable channels make the execution failed/incomplete; withhold their bytes because a cutoff can split a credential. No such draft governs review authority. Caller cancellation and CLI interrupt/termination signals stop the covered process set; pipe wait is bounded.\n1023:Inspect `safety` on the immutable run, CLI dispatch/verify/resume and the existing MCP review-bundle projection. It reports profile/platform, available/unavailable capabilities, limits, capture completeness, execution cause, runtime resource identifier and the B12 cleanup OperationResult. Cleanup verifies operation ownership and removes only the captured workspace and its exact Git registration through confined descriptors, never a global Git prune. Inventory caps are 100000 workspace entries/256MiB, 1024 registration entries/256MiB and 4096 runtime entries/128MiB, depth 128. OS filesystem calls remain subject to I/O latency; no hard syscall deadline is claimed. Failure retains uncertain resources and is separate from the domain draft. It returns an operational error, blocks authority/continuation and remains an error on idempotent replay, without another spawn. Inspect the recorded runtime identifier and registration rather than rerunning the adapter to compensate.\n1025:Retain evidence without automatic expiry (`retention_ttl_seconds: 0`); newly written run/transcript files use mode 0600 and private sessions retain their existing 0700/0600 policy. Export retained redacted run/transcript, witness, attempt/continuation receipts and optional proof together, preserving inventory and digests; exclude private sessions and issuer keys. Raw-byte digests precede redaction; retained-byte digests, canonical run identity, witness and native signature follow. No retention operation removes rejection history or restores quota. Legacy records remain readable with no fabricated safety observations. No instance policy, sandbox backend or real vendor is activated by these examples.\n1039:Pass `{session}` as an entire argv element, never inside shell code. Captures from both output channels must agree. Session references are saved under `.pose/review-private/` (directory 0700/files 0600, self-ignored by Git); keep that runtime material private. Public records contain the session digest. The supervisor redacts the captured reference from both transcript and draft before publishing; ambiguous captures withhold the unredacted bytes. Losing private material makes a run not recoverable; no replacement session is invented.\n1049:Once a scope is done, the approval a delegated run backed is verified as it was sealed: the proof's signature under an issuer that still holds its pin, the exact run record, transcript and bundle it binds, and that no later run superseded it. It is not re-verified against the repository as it is now, so a later change to a file the review sealed (the validation matrix, this manual) does not unseat it; revoking the issuer's pin, altering the record or reopening the scope does. An open scope keeps the live checks.\n1066:Use the existing native issuer and its attestation pin. Set protected `authority_project` and `authority_audience` in review policy; a declared project identity must agree. Keep keys outside the project. Dispatch captures origin/worktree, bundle/commit/scope/kind, configuration/argv/executable, identities, brief template/body/notes, planned stdin and actual pipe-write digests, raw and retained redacted output/transcript digests and completeness. A pipe write does not prove the vendor consumed the prompt. Session references and private keys stay outside the public proof.\ncodex-bwrap-synthetic-mount-targets-1000\nempty-hooks\noutput.txt\nworktree\n29:func TestArtifactPathRejectsSymlinkEscapeAndDirectory(t *testing.T) {\n36:\t\tt.Fatalf(\"symlink escape accepted: %v\", err)\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/bash -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\np=json.load(open('.pose/indexes/validation-matrix.json'))\nprint('validation config:', {k:v for k,v in p.items() if k not in ['stacks','moduleOverrides','deliveryProfiles']})\nx=json.load(open('.pose/results/delivery-validation.json'))\nprint('validation metadata:',{k:v for k,v in x.items() if k not in ['checks']})\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
